# v27 OVERLAY (user 2026-10-30, choosing options 1, 2 and 4 after v26 fell
# from 0.125 at 300k to 0.025 at 500k on Town02, and 0.050 on its own Town05).
# v26's reward exactly, with three changes. Lane invasion still ends the
# episode, and so does a collision (user rules).
. "$REPO/slurm/v26_overlay.env"

# 1. OFF-ROAD IS A FINE, NOT THE END. v26 nearly solved crossings (0.18/ep in
#    training, 3 of 40 eval endings) but 32 of 40 eval episodes ended off-road:
#    the car leaves the road at corners and, with that terminal, never
#    survives enough corners to learn them. It now pays -1 a STEP off the road
#    (EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY, inherited) -- more than a metre of driving
#    earns, so cutting a corner over the grass still loses -- and carries on.
#    An unpainted road edge was already a non-fatal (NONE) crossing; a painted
#    line stays fatal. EVAL IS UNCHANGED: _fault still ends an eval episode on
#    off-road (the user's fault-ends rule).
export EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_FATAL=0

# 2. JUNCTION GOALS RAMP 0.50 -> 0.85. v18 reached 0.725 with half its goals
#    past a junction; at 0.85 no run has beaten 0.40. The training goal sampler
#    starts at 0.50 and moves 0.05 at a time: up when training goal success is
#    >= 0.30 over 100 goal episodes at the current level, down when < 0.10.
#    JUNCTION_GOAL_FRAC (0.85, inherited) is the ceiling, and it is what the
#    EVALS keep using, so their numbers stay comparable with v22-v26.
export JUNCTION_RAMP_START=0.5 JUNCTION_RAMP_STEP=0.05
export JUNCTION_RAMP_UP=0.3 JUNCTION_RAMP_DOWN=0.1 JUNCTION_RAMP_WINDOW=100

# 4. THE SPEED GATE IS BACK (the repo's "reward is zero above target speed";
#    user removed it 2026-10-14, restores it now). Progress pays only below
#    TARGET_SPEED (20 km/h), in BOTH modes: explore's metres and goal mode's
#    route metres. Moving away from the goal is still charged at any speed, so
#    the gate cannot be farmed; HER gates hindsight rows the same way.
export PROGRESS_SPEED_GATE=1
